  "body": "Would there be a plan to introduce this shorthand, for handling an event once more easily?\r\n\r\n```js\r\nelement.once('click', e => {\r\n  console.log('click', e.target);\r\n})\r\n// vs\r\nelement.addEventListener('click', function clickHandler(e) {\r\n  element.removeEventListener('click', clickHandler);\r\n  console.log('click', e.target);\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nOne issue is the naming difference with add/removeEventListener, it would be great to shorten them to .on, .off (and possibly add this to HTMLCollection/NodeList)",
